---
description: PlayGame and ScenePlayer stay field bags with thin prototype wrappers
globs: packages/engine/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# State classes

`PlayGame` and `ScenePlayer` are bags of fields. A field stays `this.field`. Grouping fields into subobjects rewrites every read.

A method the host or a test calls stays on the prototype as one line. It calls the function in the neighboring file with `this` cast to the state type (`GameState`). The file that holds the body imports the class only as `import type`.

A method nothing outside the class calls is a plain function in that file. It leaves the prototype.

`play/index.ts` re-exports `play/game.ts` only. A new file is not added there. A symbol that callers already import from the old file is re-exported by that file.

The public paths stay: `src/index.ts`, `play/index.ts`, and the `exports` in `packages/engine/package.json`.

```ts
// Wrong: fields nested, so every former this.armed read changes.
this.input.armed = false;

// Right: the field stays on the instance. The prototype method is the wrapper.
frame(rawInput: PlayInput): void {
  return frameBody.frame.call(this as unknown as GameState, rawInput);
}
```
